 "meta": {
  "name": "Low-friction stop-junction slide across ego",
  "description": "On an apparently clear, stop-controlled junction approach, a side-approach car ignores its stop obligation and slides through the junction across the ego path under low-friction conditions. The challenger is back-solved to reach the conflict at nearly the same time as the moving ego, producing a survivable but demanding braking or pass-within-metres event.",
